@@ -803,24 +803,42 @@ the TCP path would run without the policy the mesh applied.
 
 ## L7 output and teardown
 
-Linkerd output is drained from `DmeshIo` into the DPUmesh egress arena. The tx
-waker notifies the persistent driver when new output is available.
+`DmeshIo::poll_write` synchronously reserves the DPUmesh egress arena,
+copies an accepted prefix directly from Linkerd's borrowed buffer, and commits
+it before returning. Vectored writes gather the caller's header/body slices
+into that same reservation, without a temporary payload buffer or delayed
+commit. The returned length remains one prefix across the slices. There is no intermediate TX Vec or driver payload drain.
+RX still copies staging bytes into the caller's `ReadBuf`.
 
 ```text
-Linkerd buffer → DmeshIo tx queue → DPUmesh egress arena → DMA
+Linkerd buffer → reserve / copy / commit into DPUmesh egress arena → DMA
 ```
 
-Output takes the reservation path: the adapter copies queued bytes straight
-from the endpoint into the chunk `dmesh_l7_tx_reserve` lends and publishes it
-with `dmesh_l7_tx_commit` for an exact local Pod, the origin, or an ordinary
-local choice, and `dmesh_l7_tx_commit_remote` for an exact remote Pod UID. A
-commit of `0` cancels the reservation and leaves the bytes queued, so a refusal
-costs no ordering; a negative result closes the session. When no chunk is
-available, queued bytes wait for a later driver pass.
+`dmesh_l7_tx_try_reserve` distinguishes temporary arena exhaustion (0) from an
+invalid worker, stale handle, or nested reservation (-1). A successful
+reservation is committed or cancelled exactly once. A successful commit takes
+the whole offered prefix. A zero commit returns the chunk and makes the write
+Pending; the adapter retains neither caller bytes nor the reservation pointer.
+A negative or nonzero partial commit is terminal. Remote publication retains
+its exact Pod UID and the existing peer ACK custody contract.
+
+Each endpoint is bound on its owning OS thread to the full request handle of
+one session generation. Client output explicitly routes to Origin; first and
+minted backends retain their individual Local/Remote/Any routes even before
+reply connections arrive. Close revokes these bindings before returning RX
+custody. Publication and wake callbacks run outside endpoint and quota locks.
+
+The driver gathers publication/error counters, releases consumed RX custody,
+and grants round-robin write opportunities to at most 64 sessions per pass.
+An endpoint has a 64 KiB/four-attempt allowance and all grants share a 256 KiB
+worker quota. A new epoch invalidates old allowances. Failed attempts retain
+no bytes; resource progress or the 1 ms maintenance backstop permits retry.
+Blocked writers alone are not permanent internal-ready work. Flush reports
+latched errors and does not wait for destination delivery.
 
 EOF is directional. `l7_conn_eof` closes one endpoint's input half; Linkerd may
 continue reading the reverse half and producing output. Once an endpoint has
-drained all queued bytes, the adapter retries `dmesh_l7_tx_fin` until the DPU
+closed its write half after synchronous DATA publication, the adapter retries `dmesh_l7_tx_fin` until the DPU
 accepts that ordered FIN. The paired session is retired normally only after
 both output directions published FIN. A stack endpoint that disappears before
 that two-FIN completion is a terminal failure: the adapter calls
@@ -982,7 +1000,8 @@ memory remains valid until the matching release.
 | Entry point | Result |
 |---|---|
 | `dmesh_l7_workloads` | every destination Pod this worker serves, as an inbound policy subject |
-| `dmesh_l7_tx_reserve` | writable egress-arena region or `NULL` |
+| `dmesh_l7_tx_try_reserve` | `1` reservation, `0` arena exhaustion, `-1` terminal; outputs cleared on failure |
+| `dmesh_l7_tx_reserve` | compatibility wrapper returning an arena region or `NULL` |
 | `dmesh_l7_tx_commit` | publishes a reservation or returns it unused |
 | `dmesh_l7_tx_commit_remote` | publishes a reservation to one exact remote Pod UID |
 | `dmesh_l7_tx_fin` | publishes one ordered output FIN; `0` is backpressure and is retried |
@@ -1113,3 +1132,31 @@ The L7 layer adds:
 - Linkerd output is copied once, into the DPUmesh egress arena;
 - a declined session is counted by cause; protected and unknown Services are
   refused, while a generation-known relaxed Service may continue as L4.
+
+## RDMA carrier buffer leases
+
+The optional `peer_wire_ops` TX reserve/commit/cancel and RX acquire/release
+callback groups expose the existing registered SEND/RECV slots without a
+crypto dependency. Each group must be complete; TCP continues using the copy
+API. A connection permits one outstanding lease in each direction. Tokens
+validate connection incarnation, slot, per-slot generation and direction, as
+well as the exact pointer and capacity/length. Stale or forged tokens cannot
+return another owner's slot. Generation exhaustion retires the connection.
+
+TX slots transition FREE → RESERVED → POSTED → FREE. Reserve secures SEND
+capacity; commit posts the whole nonempty prefix and never returns would-block.
+Cancel returns an unposted reservation. Only a matching successful SEND CQ
+returns a POSTED slot. RX slots transition POSTED → READY → LEASED → POSTED;
+acquire dequeues the oldest message and release reposts it. A held RX lease
+blocks later acquire/copy receives, preserving FIFO. Post/repost failures are
+terminal. Valid commit/cancel/release operations consume and clear the lease
+even on failure. QP destruction precedes MR deregistration and pool release.
+
+The compatibility functions use reserve→copy→commit and
+acquire→copy→release. Current TLS still uses these copy functions: this change
+provides the shared carrier API, while the separate TLS BIO integration and
+any future IPsec producer/consumer remain separate work. All lease calls are
+serialized on the owning worker. Callers must end leases before wire close;
+no pointer or wire handle may be used after close. Local SEND completion
+permits slot reuse, not source DELIVERED: destination REV_DONE and STREAM_ACK
+still control source custody.
